  "title": "Electric Ladyland",
  "country": "Canada",
  "released": "1979",
  "notes": "Tan Reprise Records label swith the Reprise logo in a red box and \"Manufactured and distributed by WEA Music Of Canada, Ltd. A Warner Communication Company ⓦ\" along the bottom edge.\r\n\r\nThis version comes in a gatefold jacket with twin printed inner sleeves featuring a memorial to Hendrix (\"Jimi Hendrix November 27, 1942 - September 18, 1970\"), including his discography.\r\n\r\nCat# on front and back cover: 6307\r\nCat# on interior of gatefold: 2RS 6307\r\nCat# on labels: 2 RS 6307\r\n\r\nStereo. Manufactured and distributed by WEA Music of Canada, Ltd.\r\n\r\n\"We dedicate this album to acoustic and electric woman and man alike, and to the girl at or from or with the button store, and Arizona, and Bil of some English town in England, and well, EVERYBODY.\"\r\n\r\nAll compositions published by Bella Godiva Music with the exceptions of B1 published by Joint Music, B5 published by Yameta Co., Ltd.; and D3 published by Dwarf Music.\r\n\r\nRecorded at The Record Plant, New York.\r\nReprise Records, a division of Warner Bros.-Seven Arts Records, Inc. Made in U.S.A.",
  "released_formatted": "1979",
